HTTP methods describe what action the client wants the server to perform.

Method

Purpose

Example

GET

Read data

Get all students

POST

Create new data

Add a student

PUT

Replace an existing resource

Replace student details

PATCH

Update selected fields

Update only the student's name

DELETE

Remove data

Delete a student
GET

GET retrieves information from the server.

Example:
GET /students

Expected result: a list of students.

POST

POST creates a new resource.

Example:
POST /students

Request body:

{
  "name": "Manjula",
  "course": "Information Technology"
}

PUT

PUT replaces the existing resource with the submitted data.

Example:
PUT /students/1

Request body:

{
  "name": "Manjula R",
  "course": "Information Technology"
}

PATCH

PATCH updates only the fields provided in the request.

Example:
PATCH /students/1

Request body:

{
  "name": "Manjula R"
}

DELETE

DELETE removes a resource.

Example:
DELETE /students/1
